WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.768
A strong slideshow video starts with the right number of photos — around eight for

2
00:00:05.768 --> 00:00:09.636
thirty seconds, or twelve to sixteen for a full minute.

3
00:00:09.636 --> 00:00:15.775
Choose only sharp originals, at least sixteen hundred pixels on the long side, so

4
00:00:15.775 --> 00:00:17.821
they hold up when enlarged.

5
00:00:17.821 --> 00:00:24.030
Order them as a short story: open with an establishing shot, move through the

6
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:28.061
details that matter, and close on your best image.

7
00:00:28.061 --> 00:00:33.363
Let the narration set the timing — one sentence per photo, saying what the image

8
00:00:33.363 --> 00:00:34.887
cannot show on its own.

9
00:00:34.887 --> 00:00:40.721
Add a title card, a few information cards for key facts, and a closing card for the

10
00:00:40.721 --> 00:00:41.424
next step.

11
00:00:41.424 --> 00:00:47.989
Give each photo a slow, steady zoom, keep any music quiet beneath the voice, and

12
00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:52.338
caption every word so the video works with sound off.

13
00:00:52.338 --> 00:00:58.283
Finally, export a landscape cut and a vertical cut, checking the framing on each

14
00:00:58.283 --> 00:01:00.215
format before you publish.
